{"parentUuid":"072fca32-dd66-4c22-8d01-3f7f7f06e597","isSidechain":false,"message":{"content":[{"signature":"","thinking":"Now I understand the architecture. \n\nI've identified the core mutex rule: four core operations share the same mutex, so queries during a refund batch will block until the entire batch completes. I need to add regression protection for inter-leaving two ledger handles in the same process, with the specified test scenario in mind.\n\nThe query must wait for the full batch to complete, never return outdated snapshots, and only encounter expected errors during normal waiting. The test has two deterministic outcomes: both refunds succeed (balance includes full fees, with ordered refund records) or the second persist fails (only first refund is recorded, no balance inflation, payment history remains unchanged). Post-query rechecks yield consistent state, queries are stateless, and both scenarios can be reproduced locally offline.\n\nThe current implementation already blocks queries during the batch. I’ve clarified the test workflow: create a ledger with two fee-inclusive settled payments, open a second ledger handle, inject a persist hook to trigger the two expected test scenarios.\n\nI will check the existing test infrastructure for interleaving test practices.\n","type":"thinking"}],"id":"msg_a636a7dd5dabbe7c45daf6a7","model":"auto_model/urm","role":"assistant","stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":17953,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":45880,"output_tokens":677,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"stop_details":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"type":"assistant","uuid":"5de35e3d-198f-473f-815b-119d9d84611c","timestamp":"2026-10