{"parentUuid":"1d7d51f9-cb1c-4bb2-992b-89e7f1f227f9","isSidechain":false,"message":{"content":[{"signature":"","thinking":"The .e2e directory has a prebuilt binary — not relevant to the test itself. \n\nIt has been confirmed that the existing reconcile interleave test does ensure the query will acquire the same mutex as the refund batch holds throughout its execution, so the query will wait. It is required to run `go test -race ./...` for verification. I will first create a task list and write the test file, which is modeled after the existing relevant test file with a specified USDC payment scenario.\n\nI’ve finalized the test logic and assertions. The test will cover two core scenarios: the first is handling concurrent operations during the gate blocking period, and the second is verifying the expected results after the gate release and waiting for the batch to finish.\n\nI’ve supplemented more detailed test assertions for the scenarios, clarified the verification order of test cases, and confirmed an extra step to verify that failed refunds don’t occupy subsequent valid refund sequence numbers.\n\nAdditional test requirements have been confirmed: verify that waiting queries do not error when the ledger is closed, ensure no old snapshots are returned, and mirror the Gosched() usage of the existing reconcile test. The test uses channel-based synchronization for offline determinism.\n\nI’ve decided not to add a safety timeout to avoid changing existing test habits, as existing tests will hang instead of timing out when logic is flawed. I’ll run the test with `-race` and `-count=10` to ensure stability. Query result slices are properly handled, so deep equality checks are feasible. The single account/asset scenario is kept to stay focused, and I can add a second account/asset if needed to verify balance sorting.\n\nI’ve adjusted the test scenario plan. To align with the canonical interleave test for consistency, I’ll keep the single combo scenario, and only assert the complete balances list to verify sorting.\n\nI’ve clarified the specific joint correspondence assertions required for the test, confirmed no JSON shape check is needed, and decided to place the test in the payflow package since it requires test-only package hooks not accessible to cmd tests.\n\nInterleave condition requires payflow package.\n\nI’ve confirmed the expected values for refund records, settlement records and post-refund balance metrics for the test. The core logic to verify is that failed refund sequence numbers are not occupied, which can be validated by checking the balance and refund record sequence after a subsequent successful refund. I’ll check the existing reuse test file to avoid redundant work and confirm all test requirements are met.\n","type":"thinking"}],"id":"msg_485ffabdf18b5f4c932dbda4","model":"auto_model/urm","role":"assistant","stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":11837,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":88888,"output_tokens":2148,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"stop_details":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"type":"assistant","uuid":"02ecfbef-4288-4570-92c4-94b2d2b17b1f","timestamp":"2026-10-07T06:57:00.005Z","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"12b52d87-17ec-4fe8-a0a9-321baebe2f15","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/opt/gsb-fleet/workspaces/inst-16/B/task048","sessionId":"12b52d87-17ec-4fe8-a0a9-321baebe2f15","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
